  "crossings": [
    {
      "note": "Al Kharid / Lumbridge river boundary, and the only crossing on it. Its two Gate locs are decorative -- opening them does nothing. walkTo across x=3268 is client_rejected from every tile tried until the toll dialog below is completed, at which point the same walk succeeds instantly. Confirmed live 2026-09-08. Three details each cost a session: (1) it is a TOLL costing 10 coins -- a character with an empty purse completes the whole dialog and is still refused, with no message saying why, which reads exactly like a hard block; (2) it works only from z=3227 -- all confirmed crossings depart (3264-3267, 3227) and land (3273, 3227), while z=3228 has none, so being one tile off looks like a wall; (3) the crossing hop is 6-9 tiles, longer than walkTo's ~7-8 cap, because it behaves like a dialog-gated teleport -- send ONE direct walkTo to 'beyond' rather than hopping. Because the boundary is a river, a character on the west bank north of z~3240 cannot reach the eastern corridor (x~3269-3277) by walking east at its own latitude; it is walking into water and reports 'moving but not closing on the target'. Go south to z=3227, cross, then north.",
      "x_range": [
        3260,
        3276
      ],
      "z_range": [
        3150,
        3260
      ],
      "mechanism": "dialog",
      "npc": "Border Guard",
      "beyond": [
        3273,
        3227
      ],
      "toll_coins": 10,
      "depart_z": 3227,
      "single_hop": true
    },
    {
      "note": "Lumbridge/Varrock. The southern world and the Varrock area are separate regions in this file's own recorded history: everything walked in the north was walked by a character that was already there, so for a long time no route existed between them and route.py correctly reported no_known_route. This is the crossing that links them, found by route.py --explore probing the narrowest unwalked gaps between the two regions. It is a plain walk -- no gate, door, stile or dialog -- which is why nothing in the world announces it and why only exploring found it. Confirmed live 2026-09-09. This is also, independently, the far edge of the swamp/marsh band two characters got stuck in from 2026-09-08 through 2026-09-10 approaching from the south -- the crossing sits just past where those attempts gave up: the swamp itself wasn't the route, this specific gap north of it was.",
      "x_range": [
        3186,
        3222
      ],
      "z_range": [
        3326,
        3368
      ],
      "mechanism": "walk",
      "from": [
        3219,
        3333
      ],
      "beyond": [
        3190,
        3363
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ship_gangplank",
      "mechanism": "Cross",
      "note": "Boarding and leaving any ship is a Gangplank loc whose ONLY option is Cross (opIndex 1), not Open. Confirmed live 2026-09-12 at Karamja (2956,3144 id 2082) and Port Sarim (3031,3217 id 2084). While aboard, player.level is 1; after crossing it is 0. A walker that only probes for Gate/Door/Stile reports 'stuck' on the dock tile with no idea a ship is under it.",
